 prisoner of war status, Purple Heart awards, financial need, or VA health care priority groups."],"missing_information":["Specific details on the exact definitions of each priority category referenced by section 1705(a) of title 38.","Cost estimates, funding sources, or budgetary impacts of expanding dental care to all enrolled veterans.","Projections on how many individual veterans will utilize the newly available dental services."],"plain_summary":"The Dental Care for Veterans Act expands eligibility for dental services provided by the Department of Veterans Affairs (VA) so that all veterans enrolled in the VA health care system can receive dental care in the same manner as any other medical service. Currently, only veterans with service-connected dental issues or other narrow criteria qualify. The bill phases in this expanded eligibility over four years based on existing categories of VA health care eligibility.","significance":"The bill changes how dental care is integrated into veterans' overall health benefits by transitioning dental services from a restricted benefit for specific conditions to a standard medical service available to all enrolled veterans over a four-year rollout."},"summary_meta":{"generated_at":"2026-10-26T13:15:20+00:00","model":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","source_basis":"text+summary","source_urls":["https://www.congress.gov/119/bills/hr210/BILLS-119hr210ih.htm"]},"summary_threshold":50,"title":"Dental Care for Veterans Act","viability":48.1,"viability_detail":{"breakdown":[{"available":true,"effective_weight":35.0,"inputs":[{"label":"Detected stage","value":"Reported by committee"}],"key":"stage","label":"Legislative stage","note":"Stage value from the table on the About page.","points":21.0,"value":0.6,"weight":35},{"available":true,"effective_weight":15.0,"inputs":[{"label":"Committee activity","value":"Reported out of committee (or past committee stage)"}],"key":"committee","label":"Committee activity","note":"","points":15.0,"value":1.0,